WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.805
Although this is a theory paper without
experimental ablations,

00:00:03.885 --> 00:00:08.491
the analysis is structured to expose which
assumptions buy which guarantees,

00:00:08.571 --> 00:00:10.649
playing the role an ablation would.

00:00:10.729 --> 00:00:15.952
The single upper-bound argument is versatile enough
to recover the earlier square-root

00:00:16.032 --> 00:00:20.022
OPT rate for general well-behaved distributions as
a special case,

00:00:20.102 --> 00:00:25.078
and crucially it also goes through for the hinge
loss, not just the logistic loss;

00:00:25.158 --> 00:00:29.272
this dual applicability is what enables the
perceptron second phase.

00:00:29.352 --> 00:00:33.588
The theorem cleanly separates the bounded and
sub-exponential regimes,

00:00:33.668 --> 00:00:38.891
showing that the only price of moving from bounded
to heavier sub-exponential tails is

00:00:38.971 --> 00:00:41.604
an extra logarithmic factor in one over OPT.

00:00:41.684 --> 00:00:46.229
Likewise, the constant Cκ, an integral of the
radial-Lipschitzness modulus,

00:00:46.309 --> 00:00:50.299
isolates exactly how much the density's radial
smoothness matters,

00:00:50.379 --> 00:00:53.320
vanishing when the density is radially symmetric.
